I went on a magical trip that changed my  life forever  and this is that story so it's Labor Day  weekend 2016 and my friend tells me she  has an update on my ex so I'm just like  oh my god what's going on does he have a  girlfriend already she tells me no no  girlfriend so I am relieved but then she  tells me that he recently went to Japan  that pissed me off so much because my ex  does not like to travel I had to book  all of our trips together he went to  Puerto Rico we went to Mexico City it  was all because of the work that I did  to plan these trips and one of the big  trips I wanted to do for us was to go to  Tokyo it's been my dream trip since I  was a kid so fueled my Instagram  jealousy I ran back to my apartment and  immediately began googling trips to  Japan I found round-trip tickets for  $750 whoo then I texted my childhood  friend Pat and I told about this crazy  cheap deal that I found he was down I  was down we decided to spend two weeks  in Japan a month after we booked our  flights my father was hospitalized due  to complications with diabetes I was  with my dad at the hospital for most of  the time and I assumed the role of the  caregiver because my mother is a nanny  and she does not have the same  flexibility as I do work in here  buzzfeed we received the heavy news that  he was diagnosed with kidney cancer I  never thought that I'd be in a situation  where either my parents would have  cancer I took my dad to two different  oncologists they both agreed he needed a  tumor removed from his left kidney I  somehow miraculously got him into one of  the best hospitals in the country but I  was getting nervous the trip to Japan  was getting closer and closer and I  wasn't at work a lot and I asked my boss  at one point should I still go to Japan  is that okay she said please go you need  to travel and get your mind off things  and with my family and boss's blessing I  hopped on a plane with my friend Pat and  we embarked to the Land of the Rising  Sun we started our trip in Kyoto which  is Japan's aging capital it has  thousands of temples and shrines so we  decided to book an all-day tour so we  can hit up all the important spots  obviously at the time I had a lot going  on my life  and also a very spiritual person so it's  important to me when I was in Kyoto to  pray in these temples and shrines and  doing a very respectful manner at the  end of this tour I'm totally nerding out  I'm in the front of the group asking all  the annoying questions raising my hand  it got to a point where I was that  person holding the tour guide pole I was  that tourist and all of a sudden I  noticed this cute guy and I think he's  looking at me at one point we locked  eyes and then I looked away because I  just thought he was staring at me  because I looked crazy with that tour  Pole thing so we're at the last stop of  the tour and it's this magical temple  called Q Mizzou Dera it's absolutely  stunning there are these two stones and  they're actually called the love stones  and legend goes that you must close your  eyes and walk from one stone to another  stone and if you're able to walk from  one stone to another stone with your  eyes closed without any help that means  you won't need help finding love however  if you off from one stone to the other  stone and you need help  you will need help finding love whether  it's a matchmaker your mom tinder you're  gonna need help so my friend Pat walks  from one stone to the other they're  about 60 feet apart and he is flawless I  do it and I'm a hot mess I trip I  stumble  yeah in other words I desperately need  help finding love before we knew it it  was time to head back to the tour bus  and go back to our hotels so as I get  back in the bus  I noticed that that really cute guy who  I thought was checking me out  he was sitting the back of the bus - it  was weird because he definitely wasn't  sitting the back of the bus throughout  the whole day of this tour so here I'm  talking about traveling and where he's  been in Japan so I turn around and start  talking to him we're hitting it off he  introduced himself as Josh I told him I  was Alexis and then I quickly introduced  them to Pat but I made sure to say this  is my friend Pat so he knew I was  traveling with a homie and not a  boyfriend so then I gave my Instagram  handle and I told him to follow me which  he did I became friends with this girl  named Molly from Australia and we made  plans to hang out that night so I  figured I'd asked Josh to join us cuz  he's also an Aussie why not  Molly Josh and I mean the hotel lobby  that evening and I lead them to this  really cool ramen place that I found on  Yelp we had a great meal inside to get  drinks afterwards which is where things  took a turn after a few hours in a bar I  propose that we do karaoke because Japan  is the birthplace of karaoke you know  that chemistry you have when you go out  with a crush your arms are brushing each  other  your legs are rubbing next to each other  and you feel that spark in the air  that's how it felt  singing with Josh Molly finally leaves  to go to the bathroom the second Molly  leaves a room Josh and I begin looking  each other and we just start immediately  kissing 4:00 a.m. rolls around and we  leave the karaoke bar after we dropped  off Molly Josh and I headed straight to  his hotel the next morning we woke up  together and ate a hungover lunch at  McDonald's we ended up spending the  whole day together and we've really  opened up about our lives he tells me  that his parents are both cancer  survivors so I told about my dad's  recent cancer diagnosis and we really  really really bonded over that Josh and  I spent 36 hours together and the only  reason we stopped hanging out was  because he had to go back home to  Australia I still had a week left in  Japan so I finally met up with tad again  for him all the while Josh and I kept  talking on whatsapp it felt like he was  my boyfriend even though he wasn't  eventually my trip to Japan ends I'm  back in New York City a few random guys  my past asked me to hang out and it  frustrated me these boys were playing  themselves I hadn't heard from them in  months and they just started popping up  on my trip after Japan and it just gave  me clarity that really the only person  he wants to be with was Josh a few days  later I was on the phone with Josh and I  just told him the truth I was like look  I only want to be with you and no one  else oh my god I was feeling the same  way if I was in a wait until Christmas  to tell you that he said it felt really  nice that we were both in the same page  so we both laughed and like decided then  and there that after 36 hours of hanging  out he was my boyfriend and I was his  girlfriend fast forward to a month later  my father was about to get surgery to  have his tumor removed my father is a  man of God and I grew up in a Baptist  Church and I really respect and love the  power of prayer but nothing had prepared  me for my father's surgery update a few  days after surgery my father's doctor  called and he said that my dad's tumor  was benign I thought back to two things  I distinctly prayed for in Kyoto first  was my father's health I I prayed for a  speedy recovery like I wouldn't be the  optimistic woman that I am today if it  wasn't for him so that was a really it  was a really important prayer in Kyoto  the second thing I prayed for in Kyoto  was true love so here I am my mid-30s  and I prayed to find true love no matter  my age I was like if I find true love my  40s or 50s or 60s I'd be okay with it I  just want to find the right person I'm  sure you're wondering what's going on  with Josh and I now well  I end up going to Australia to meet his  friends and family and he came to New  York City to meet mine less than a year  after we met he moved to LA we got  engaged exactly a year after we met we  went to the Beverly Hills courthouse and  got married and it only cost us $90 to  get married what a steal I never gave up  on love and it led me to where I am now  I hope the one thing you can take away  from this video is to do the same don't  give up on love  [Music]
 

